# Spotler Mail+ Product Context Skill

## Purpose

Use this Skill when designing or redesigning product features for Spotler Mail+.

This Skill gives Figma Make product context for Spotler Mail+ so it can make better UX and product decisions without starting from generic SaaS assumptions. It explains what the product is, who uses it, how it works, which workflows matter, which terminology to use, and what product logic should be preserved.

This is not a Design System Skill. Do not use this Skill for visual styling, component rules, typography, spacing, colours, or layout patterns. Use the separate Spotler Design System Skill or attached design system documentation for those decisions.

---

## Product Summary

Spotler Mail+ is an email marketing solution for organisations that use email as an important communication channel.

It helps marketing and communications teams create professional newsletters, automate follow-ups, personalise email content, manage audiences, monitor deliverability, and understand campaign performance from one structured environment.

Spotler Mail+ is built for teams that want both speed and control. It supports reusable templates, brand settings, dynamic content, segmentation, automated campaigns, CRM and CDP synchronisation, engagement tracking, A/B testing, and reporting.

The product helps teams move from manual, inconsistent, and generic email production to a more structured, data-driven, and scalable email workflow.

---

## Core Problem Spotler Mail+ Solves

Spotler Mail+ solves several connected problems for marketing and communications teams.

### 1. Email production takes too much manual work

Many teams spend too much time building emails, recreating content blocks, applying brand styling manually, reviewing versions, and making last-minute changes.

Spotler Mail+ reduces this work through:

- Drag-and-drop email creation
- Reusable templates
- Reusable content blocks
- Brand settings
- Pre-send checks
- Previews
- AI support for content and subject lines

The goal is to help teams create branded emails faster while reducing errors and inconsistencies.

### 2. Email campaigns are often too generic

Many organisations send the same message to broad lists, even when they have customer, behavioural, CRM, or CDP data available.

Spotler Mail+ supports more relevant email communication through:

- Static and dynamic lists
- Tags
- Scoring
- Profile data
- Behavioural data
- CRM-based segmentation
- CDP-driven segmentation
- Dynamic content blocks
- Personalised campaign flows

The goal is to send more relevant messages to the right audience at the right time.

### 3. Follow-up is difficult to scale manually

After downloads, sign-ups, abandoned carts, booking interest, or other interactions, timely follow-up matters. Manual follow-up is inconsistent and hard to scale.

Spotler Mail+ supports automated email sequences based on:

- Behaviour
- Dates
- List changes
- Customer data
- Product data
- CRM or CDP signals

The goal is to automate timely follow-up while keeping campaigns manageable for marketers.

### 4. Deliverability and list quality limit campaign results

Even well-designed emails fail if they do not reach the inbox or if lists are poorly maintained.

Spotler Mail+ supports deliverability and list management through:

- Domain authentication support
- SPF
- DKIM
- DMARC
- Engagement filtering
- List management
- Suppression tools
- Privacy and compliance support

The goal is to improve sustainable inbox placement and long-term engagement.

### 5. Marketing and sales data are often disconnected

For B2B organisations, campaign engagement is more valuable when it is visible in the CRM and usable by sales.

Spotler Mail+ supports CRM synchronisation and can write engagement such as opens and clicks back to contact level.

The goal is to align marketing and sales around the same contact data and engagement signals.

---

## Target Users and User Roles

Spotler Mail+ is primarily used by marketing and communications teams in SME and mid-market organisations.

### Primary users

#### Email marketer

An email marketer creates, sends, automates, measures, and optimises email campaigns.

Goals:

- Build branded emails quickly
- Segment audiences
- Personalise content
- Automate follow-up
- Improve engagement and conversion
- Understand campaign performance

Typical needs:

- Drag-and-drop editing
- Reusable templates
- Dynamic content
- List and segment management
- Campaign scheduling
- Reporting and A/B testing

---

#### Marketing manager

A marketing manager oversees campaign planning, brand consistency, audience strategy, and performance.

Goals:

- Maintain quality and brand control
- Improve campaign efficiency
- Increase conversion and customer value
- Reduce manual work
- Align campaigns with customer lifecycle stages

Typical needs:

- Campaign overview
- Active and draft campaign visibility
- Performance trends
- Clear approval or pre-send confidence
- Reusable templates and brand settings

---

#### Communications professional

A communications professional uses Mail+ for newsletters, stakeholder updates, public communications, and regular announcements.

Goals:

- Send professional newsletters
- Maintain consistent messaging
- Segment stakeholders or audiences
- Automate date-based reminders
- Monitor engagement

Typical needs:

- Easy email creation
- Templates
- Audience lists
- Scheduling
- Reports
- Reliable deliverability

---

#### CRM or B2B campaign marketer

A CRM or B2B marketer uses Mail+ with CRM data to target prospects, leads, and customers.

Goals:

- Use CRM segments in campaigns
- Write engagement back to the CRM
- Support lead nurturing
- Align marketing and sales
- Help sales prioritise follow-up

Typical needs:

- CRM-synchronised lists
- Contact-level engagement data
- Lead nurturing flows
- Segmentation by sector, stage, or customer status
- Campaign reporting connected to sales follow-up

---

#### E-commerce marketer

An e-commerce marketer uses Mail+ to combine newsletters, product data, customer behaviour, and automated lifecycle campaigns.

Goals:

- Increase conversion
- Recover abandoned carts or browsing sessions
- Send product-related campaigns
- Reactivate customers
- Personalise content with CDP or webshop data

Typical needs:

- Product data integration
- CDP connection
- Dynamic content
- Abandoned cart and browse flows
- Back-in-stock and price-drop campaigns
- Post-purchase follow-up

---

### Secondary users

#### Deliverability or technical specialist

A deliverability or technical specialist may support domain setup, authentication, data flows, and integrations.

Goals:

- Ensure reliable inbox placement
- Configure authentication
- Support list hygiene
- Connect CRM, CDP, webshop, or API integrations

Typical needs:

- SPF, DKIM, and DMARC setup visibility
- Deliverability guidance
- Sync status
- Integration monitoring
- Suppression and engagement filtering tools

---

#### Sales user or sales manager

A sales user may not work directly in Mail+ every day, but benefits from campaign engagement being written back to the CRM.

Goals:

- See which contacts opened or clicked campaigns
- Prioritise follow-up
- Understand lead interest
- Align sales activity with marketing engagement

Typical needs:

- Contact-level engagement history
- CRM feedback
- Clear campaign interaction signals

