## Important Product Objects and Concepts

### Email

A message created and sent through Mail+. It may be part of a one-off campaign or an automated sequence.

### Newsletter

A recurring or regular email communication, often used for updates, promotions, content, or stakeholder communication.

### Campaign

A planned email or SMS communication sent to a selected audience. A campaign may be one-off or part of a wider workflow.

### Automated campaign

A campaign that runs based on triggers, dates, list changes, behaviour, or data signals.

### Flow or workflow

An automated sequence of steps, usually involving triggers, waits, conditions, and follow-up emails.

### Template

A reusable email structure that helps users create branded emails faster and more consistently.

### Content block

A reusable piece of email content that can be inserted into emails, such as a header, product block, CTA section, article section, or footer.

### Brand manager

A product area for managing brand settings such as colours, typography, and buttons. This helps maintain consistent branding across campaigns.

### List

A group of contacts used for targeting email campaigns. Lists may be static or dynamic.

### Static list

A list that contains a fixed or manually managed set of contacts.

### Dynamic list

A list that updates based on rules, data, behaviour, tags, CRM data, or CDP data.

### Tag

A label applied to contacts based on interest, behaviour, engagement, survey answers, or other criteria.

### Score

A value that indicates interest, engagement, or lead quality.

### Contact

A person who can receive email or SMS communication. Contacts may contain profile data, preferences, engagement history, tags, scores, and CRM/CDP attributes.

### Contact-level engagement

Engagement data such as opens and clicks stored at the individual contact level. This is important for CRM feedback and sales follow-up.

### Segment

A targeted group of contacts selected by list membership, tags, profile data, behaviour, CRM data, CDP data, or preferences.

### Dynamic content block

A content block that changes depending on contact data, segment, preference, behaviour, or profile attributes.

### Trigger

An event or condition that starts an automated campaign or workflow step.

### Suppression

A mechanism to prevent specific contacts from receiving messages, often for unsubscribe, compliance, list hygiene, or deliverability reasons.

### Engagement filtering

Filtering based on whether contacts are active, inactive, engaged, or unengaged.

### Deliverability

The ability of emails to reach recipients’ inboxes reliably.

### Domain authentication

Technical setup that supports sender trust and deliverability, including SPF, DKIM, and DMARC.

### A/B test

A test comparing two or more versions of subject lines or content to determine which performs better.

### Mailing report

A report showing results for a specific mailing or campaign.

### Trend report

A report showing performance patterns over time.

